msgid "header.subtitle"
msgstr "no meeting starts before the muppets"

msgid "header.introduction"
msgstr "Imagine sitting down for a meeting, saying good morning, and then just... starting. No muppets. Nobody made anything. 😬"

msgid "example.character.neutral.name"
msgstr "Tim"

msgid "example.character.neutral.avatar-description"
msgstr "Tim's Slack avatar"

msgid "example.character.bad.name"
msgstr "Keith"

msgid "example.character.bad.avatar-description"
msgstr "Keith's Slack avatar"

msgid "example.character.good.name"
msgstr "Dawn"

msgid "example.character.good.avatar-description"
msgstr "Dawn's Slack avatar"

msgid "example.bad.title"
msgstr "❌ Don't do this"

# the placeholder is the year, i.e. "2026"
msgid "example.bad.body"
msgstr ""
"Keith just tried to run a meeting without showing a single piece of Muppet-themed art. This is not how meetings work, and it hasn't been since %1$s.\n"
"\n"
"The muppet requirement isn't red tape - it's the whole point. A meeting without muppets is just people staring at each other, waiting to be disappointed.\n"
"\n"
"The same goes for:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Let's just dive in.\"\n"
"- \"I'll send something later.\"\n"
"- \"Can we skip that part today?\"\n"
"- \"I forgot, next time I promise.\"\n"
"- etc.\n"
"\n"
"**No muppets, no meeting.** 😫\n"

msgid "example.bad.message1.timestamp"
msgstr "9:00 AM"

msgid "example.bad.message1.body"
msgstr "ok let's get started"

msgid "example.bad.reply1.timestamp"
msgstr "9:00 AM"

msgid "example.bad.reply1.body"
msgstr "wait - where's your muppet art?"

msgid "example.bad.message2.timestamp"
msgstr "9:01 AM"

msgid "example.bad.message2.body"
msgstr "I didn't make any"

msgid "example.bad.reply2.timestamp"
msgstr "9:01 AM"

msgid "example.bad.reply2.body"
msgstr "then we're not starting"

msgid "example.good.title"
msgstr "✅ Instead try this"

msgid "example.good.body"
msgstr ""
"It doesn't have to be good art. **It just has to feature the Muppets.**\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"- a crayon drawing of a frog taped to your webcam\n"
"- a five-second sketch on a sticky note\n"
"- a felt puppet you made that's \"inspired by\" a pig\n"
"- etc.\n"
"\n"
"Showing the art first means everyone in the meeting starts from the same place: **the muppets have been acknowledged.** Skip it, and the meeting cannot proceed.\n"
"\n"
"When done right - everyone's happy! 🎉\n"

msgid "example.good.message1.timestamp"
msgstr "9:00 AM"

msgid "example.good.message1.body"
msgstr "morning! before we start - my muppet art"

msgid "example.good.reply1.timestamp"
msgstr "9:00 AM"

msgid "example.good.reply1.body"
msgstr "there it is. now we can begin"

msgid "example.good.message2.timestamp"
msgstr "9:01 AM"

msgid "example.good.message2.body"
msgstr "great, let's get started"

msgid "example.good.reply2.timestamp"
msgstr "9:01 AM"

msgid "example.good.reply2.body"
msgstr "🎉"

msgid "footer.note"
msgstr "This is kinda only half serious (kinda 👀) so please don't get mad at the person who sent you here."

msgid "footer.warning"
msgstr "That said, if you see this site's URL in a meeting invite, be prepared to be turned away if you show up without muppets."

msgid "footer.thanks"
msgstr "A fork of the wonderful [nohello.net](https://nohello.net/). Avatars taken from *[The Office](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Office_(British_TV_series))*. Open-source on [GitHub](https://github.com/sirredbeard/yesmuppetsnet). Not affiliated with Disney or The Muppets Studio."

# prefix before a list of languages, i.e. This site is available in: English, French, & German
msgid "footer.languages"
msgstr "This site is available in:"
